# Gradescope autograder build artifact (regenerate with
# build-gradescope-autograder.sh; never commit the zip)
autograder.zip

# Development trace capture — runtime state, never committed
.test-run-state/
.test-runs.log

# Claude Code session-local state: observer logs, observations, ephemeral
# plans, scheduled-task locks, machine-specific settings. Not shared across
# instructor checkouts.
#
# Ignore .claude contents by default, then re-include the parts that are
# shared instructor tooling: agent definitions, hooks, skills, and the
# project-level hook wiring. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so this must be `.claude/*` and not `.claude/` for
# the negations to have any effect. Without them a file added under
# .claude/skills/ is silently untracked — present locally, absent from a
# fresh clone — which is how the project-design skill first landed.
# settings.local.json stays ignored: it is machine-specific.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json

# Git worktrees created for isolated feature development. Worktree contents
# should never be tracked — each worktree has its own branch.
.worktrees/

# Superpowers brainstorming companion: persisted mockups + server state.
# Per-session ephemera; nothing here belongs in shared history.
.superpowers/

# Raw (unredacted) AI transcripts. Hooks and ingest write verbatim vendor
# artifacts here; the capture layer then commits a REDACTED derivative at
# .ai-traces/<tool>/redacted/ (see tests/_capture/redaction.py and
# AI_POLICY.md). This pattern is `.ai-traces/*/raw/` and NOT `.ai-traces/`:
# heartbeat/, redacted/, normalized/ and capture-health.json must stay
# committed, or the "evidence but no heartbeat" signal disappears.
.ai-traces/*/raw/

# Codex CLI credentials -- never commit OpenAI tokens. AI trace JSONL files
# under .ai-traces/ ARE committed by design (see PROCESS_TRACKING.md and
# AI_POLICY.md). .codex/config.toml, .codex/hooks.json and .codex/hooks/ are
# also committed because they are shipped (and hash-pinned) by the
# instructor. This single exclusion protects only the auth blob.
.codex/auth.json

# Aider CLI transcript files (.aider.chat.history.md, .aider.input.history)
# and its repo-map cache directory (.aider.tags.cache.v3/). Pre-adding this
# pattern means aider's own auto-append-to-.gitignore behavior is a no-op
# (aider skips the append when a matching pattern already exists), so aider
# users never mutate this pinned file and trip the integrity check. The
# chat/input history files are still captured into auto-track snapshots via
# the aider adapter's force_paths() -- see tests/_capture/agent_adapters/aider.py.
.aider*
